infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Three traps of an async DB validator (rising severity)
  order asc
  sequences
    - label DI — the injected repo is undefined
      desc Forget useContainer and class-validator instantiates the constraint outside Nest's DI, so this.users is undefined. A deploy-day crash, easy to find.
    - label Perf + a user-enumeration oracle
      desc A DB round trip on every request before the handler; a distinct email-taken 400 lets an attacker enumerate which emails have accounts. Mitigate with rate limiting and a vague message.
    - label TOCTOU race — the real lesson
      desc Read-then-write: two concurrent signups both SELECT absent, both pass, both INSERT — duplicate rows or an unhandled 500. Only a UNIQUE index serializes them; map 23505 to a 409.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b #f43f5e
